* Dogfood task 2026-07-18: device descriptor pairing dogfm.a's "dogfm"
* custom file manager with a driver name, per os9-systems-dev's
* device-drivers.md Device Descriptor Fields table -- same working
* pattern as the earlier dogfood-driver-loopback-desc.a (Devic=$0F
* module type, 6-operand psect, 12-byte psect-header-padding gap that
* shifts every field below $30 to landing 12 bytes later in the file,
* double-quoted string literals only). Full account:
* dogfood-report-filemgr-2026-07-18.md.
*
* M$FMgr points at "dogfm" (this session's custom file manager,
* dogfm.a) instead of "SCF". M$PDev points at "dogloop" (the earlier
* session's driver name) purely to have a plausible driver name in the
* field -- since driver dispatch was already found broken, and this
* session is testing file-manager dispatch specifically, no actual
* working driver is required for the experiment to be meaningful:
* IO_Type()'s path classification (see dogfm.a's header) happens
* before any device-descriptor field is ever consulted, driver or
* file-manager alike.
*
* VERIFICATION STATUS (see report for full detail):
*   - Assembles clean (0 errors) with double-quoted string literals
*     (same r68 gotcha found in the driver session -- single-quoted
*     strings fail with "*** error - value out of range ***").
*   - Links clean; `ident` confirms "68000 Dev Descr, Object Code,
*     Sharable, System State Process", Ty/La=$F01, Attr/Rev=$A001.
*   - Live: `load`ed resident as "DOGFM2" (confirmed via `mdir`).
*     `iniz DOGFM2` silently no-ops (no error, `devs` stays an empty
*     table). `dir /DOGFM2` and dogfmtest.a's real `I$Open("/DOGFM2")`
*     both fail with the identical error the driver session's
*     `/DOGFOOD` hit: Error #000:221 (E$MNF) Module Not Found -- see
*     dogfm.a's header for the source-level reason this is provably
*     the same underlying wall, not just an empirically similar one.
* ============================================================

 nam dogfmdesc
 ttl DOGFM2 device descriptor -- pairs dogfm file manager with a driver name

Devic    set $0F
Objct    set $01
ReEnt    set $80
SuperSt  set $20
Type_Lang set (Devic<<8)+Objct
Attr_Rev  set ((ReEnt+SuperSt)<<8)+1

 psect dogfmdesc,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,1,0,0

dogfmdesc:
 dc.l  0            * M$Port    -- no real hardware, 0
 dc.b  0            * M$Vector  -- no IRQ
 dc.b  0            * M$IRQLvl
 dc.b  0            * M$Prior
 dc.b  $03          * M$Mode: bit0 read + bit1 write
 dc.w  fmgrname     * M$FMgr -- offset to "dogfm" string
 dc.w  drvname      * M$PDev -- offset to "dogloop" string
 dc.w  0            * M$DevCon -- no config table
 dc.l  0            * reserved (first 4 of 8)
 dc.l  0            * reserved (second 4 of 8)
 dc.w  0            * M$Opt -- 0-byte options table

fmgrname:
 dc.b  "dogfm"
 dc.b  0
drvname:
 dc.b  "dogloop"
 dc.b  0

 ends
